Implemented the Firmware Compliance Gate accuracy changes in `/home/administrator/infra-config-portal`.

Key changes:
- Added Cisco console-based firmware inventory using read-only `show version`, with IOS XE parsing and redacted report output.
- Added numeric IOS XE version comparison tests for `17.15.05`, `17.9.1`, and `17.6.5`.
- Added scoped firmware compliance for `hpe`, `cisco`, `netapp`, and `full`.
- Updated gate behavior so NetApp `not_configured_yet` does not block Cisco or HPE scopes, but remains visible for full certification.
- Added Make targets:
  - `provider-lab-firmware-cisco-inventory`
  - `provider-lab-firmware-compliance-scope-cisco`
  - `provider-lab-firmware-compliance-scope-hpe`
  - `provider-lab-firmware-compliance-scope-full`
- Updated UI data shown for firmware scope and Cisco source.
- Saved final report: `artifacts/codex-runs/firmware-gate-accuracy-report.md`

Real-lab rerun results:
- Cisco inventory: blocked because the serial port opened but no prompt text was captured, so no fresh IOS XE version could be parsed.
- Cisco scope: blocked only by Cisco IOS XE unknown. Next action now says: `Run Cisco firmware inventory from console.`
- HPE scope: warning-only; iLO passed at `iLO 5 v3.19`; NetApp did not block HPE scope.
- Full scope: blocked as expected, with Cisco unknown and NetApp `not_configured_yet` visible.

Verification:
- `cd app/backend && PROVIDER_MODE=mock PYTHONPATH=. .venv/bin/pytest -q tests/test_firmware_compliance.py tests/test_provider_status_adapters.py`: 98 passed.
- `cd app/frontend && npm run build`: passed.
- I did not capture UI screenshots; I verified the frontend with a production build, but did not launch the dev server during this real-lab run.

No firmware updates were performed, no privileged Cisco exec was required for `show version`, and `.env.local.real-lab` contents were not printed.


